abstract: "gazahomes is an R package for exploring nine published aggregate indicators from a study of 302 participating households in Gaza. It pairs each indicator with an English–Arabic question dictionary, its applicable denominator and source references. Users can reproduce the reported percentages and reconcile denominators with documented exclusions. The archive contains no participant-level records. The study used non-probability sampling, and the estimates describe the participating households only. The MIT license covers the package code, tests and help pages. CC BY 4.0 covers the released tables, descriptions, selection and arrangement to the extent of the licensor’s rights."
